{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1772835792673,"sessionID":"ses_33ac0a501ffe2fz58zJYBeFUqb","part":{"id":"prt_cc53f6618001N97EFjlxoHNSf1","sessionID":"ses_33ac0a501ffe2fz58zJYBeFUqb","messageID":"msg_cc53f5bd70012QLSZyS8zCoQR0","type":"tool","callID":"call_function_d73low5f205w_1","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/paule/MAD/.tmp/webui-key-prompt.instructions"},"output":"<path>/home/paule/MAD/.tmp/webui-key-prompt.instructions</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: You are a QA engineer writing a test specification from a feature plan.\n2: \n3: ## Feature: webui key prompt\n4: \n5: ### Plan:\n6: I'll explore the codebase to understand the current implementation and create a comprehensive plan that addresses all the issues raised in the review feedback.\n7: Now let me check the template structure in index.html:\n8: Now I have a complete understanding of the codebase. Let me create a comprehensive plan that addresses all the issues identified in the review feedback.\n9: \n10: ```json\n11: {\n12:   \"questions\": [],\n13:   \"plan\": \"# WebUI Key Authentication Implementation Plan\\n\\n## Overview\\nImplement a modal overlay prompting for the dashboard key, stored in localStorage. Without a valid key, the backend must not send any actual data to the frontend.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 1: Fix Critical Modal Rendering Bug\\n\\n**Issue**: The key modal (index.html lines 250-257) is INSIDE the `{{if .Authenticated}}` block (line 210). Unauthenticated users see a blank page.\\n\\n**Solution**:\\n1. Restructure index.html to move key modal outside the `{{if .Authenticated}}` block\\n2. Add a separate `{{if .ShowKeyModal}}` or unconditionally render the modal container\\n3. Use JavaScript to show/hide the modal based on auth state\\n\\n**Implementation**:\\n- Move modal HTML to appear BEFORE the `{{if .Authenticated}}` conditional in index.html\\n- Keep modal in its own conditional that evaluates independently of authenticated state\\n- Backend passes `DashboardKeyConfigured` boolean to template (not just `Authenticated`)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 2: Fix Data Leakage - Server-Side Auth Enforcement\\n\\n**Issue**: api.go:139-153 fetches ALL clients/features before checking auth. Data is sent to browser but hidden with CSS.\\n\\n**Solution**:\\n1. Modify the root handler (api.go:125-159) to check authentication BEFORE fetching data\\n2. If not authenticated, render minimal page with modal but NO client/feature data\\n3. Return appropriate HTTP status (401) for API calls without valid key\\n\\n**Implementation**:\\n```go\\n// In registerRoutes, for \"/\" handler (api.go:125-159)\\nkey := r.URL.Query().Get(\\\"key\\\")\\nauthenticated := key != \\\"\\\" && (cfg.DashboardKey == \\\"\\\" || key == cfg.DashboardKey)\\n\\nif !authenticated {\\n    // Only render modal, no data\\n    data := map[string]interface{}{\\n        \\\"Key\\\":           \\\"\\\",\\n        \\\"Authenticated\\\": false,\\n        \\\"ShowKeyModal\\\":  cfg.DashboardKey != \\\"\\\", // Always show modal when key is required\\n        \\\"Clients\\\":       []Client{}, // Empty data\\n        \\\"StageGroups\\\":   []... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n14: }\n15: ```\n16: \n17: ---\n18: \n19: ## Test Spec Requirements\n20: \n21: Write a comprehensive test spec with these sections:\n22: \n23: ### 1. Behaviors That MUST Be Verified\n24: - Each behavior from the plan\n25: - Success criteria for each\n26: - Expected outputs\n27: \n28: ### 2. Edge Cases\n29: - Empty/null inputs\n30: - Boundary conditions\n31: - Invalid states\n32: - Concurrent operations\n33: - Error conditions\n34: \n35: ### 3. What Constitutes Failure\n36: - Criteria for test failure\n37: - Error messages expected\n38: - Rollback behavior\n39: \n40: ### 4. Out of Scope\n41: - Explicitly list what NOT to test (UI timing, visual assertions, performance benchmarks, etc.)\n42: \n43: ---\n44: \n45: Write in plain language, NOT actual test code. Focus on \"what should happen\" not \"how to test it\".\n\n(End of file - total 45 lines)\n</content>","title":".tmp/webui-key-prompt.instructions","metadata":{"preview":"You are a QA engineer writing a test specification from a feature plan.\n\n## Feature: webui key prompt\n\n### Plan:\nI'll explore the codebase to understand the current implementation and create a comprehensive plan that addresses all the issues raised in the review feedback.\nNow let me check the template structure in index.html:\nNow I have a complete understanding of the codebase. Let me create a comprehensive plan that addresses all the issues identified in the review feedback.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"questions\": [],\n  \"plan\": \"# WebUI Key Authentication Implementation Plan\\n\\n## Overview\\nImplement a modal overlay prompting for the dashboard key, stored in localStorage. Without a valid key, the backend must not send any actual data to the frontend.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 1: Fix Critical Modal Rendering Bug\\n\\n**Issue**: The key modal (index.html lines 250-257) is INSIDE the `{{if .Authenticated}}` block (line 210). Unauthenticated users see a blank page.\\n\\n**Solution**:\\n1. Restructure index.html to move key modal outside the `{{if .Authenticated}}` block\\n2. Add a separate `{{if .ShowKeyModal}}` or unconditionally render the modal container\\n3. Use JavaScript to show/hide the modal based on auth state\\n\\n**Implementation**:\\n- Move modal HTML to appear BEFORE the `{{if .Authenticated}}` conditional in index.html\\n- Keep modal in its own conditional that evaluates independently of authenticated state\\n- Backend passes `DashboardKeyConfigured` boolean to template (not just `Authenticated`)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Phase 2: Fix Data Leakage - Server-Side Auth Enforcement\\n\\n**Issue**: api.go:139-153 fetches ALL clients/features before checking auth. Data is sent to browser but hidden with CSS.\\n\\n**Solution**:\\n1. Modify the root handler (api.go:125-159) to check authentication BEFORE fetching data\\n2. If not authenticated, render minimal page with modal but NO client/feature data\\n3. Return appropriate HTTP status (401) for API calls without valid key\\n\\n**Implementation**:\\n```go\\n// In registerRoutes, for \"/\" handler (api.go:125-159)\\nkey := r.URL.Query().Get(\\\"key\\\")\\nauthenticated := key != \\\"\\\" && (cfg.DashboardKey == \\\"\\\" || key == cfg.DashboardKey)\\n\\nif !authenticated {\\n    // Only render modal, no data\\n    data := map[string]interface{}{\\n        \\\"Key\\\":           \\\"\\\",\\n        \\\"Authenticated\\\": false,\\n        \\\"ShowKeyModal\\\":  cfg.DashboardKey != \\\"\\\", // Always show modal when key is required\\n        \\\"Clients\\\":       []Client{}, // Empty data\\n        \\\"StageGroups\\\":   []... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Test Spec Requirements\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1772835792663,"end":1772835792672}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The user wants me to read a specific file and follow the instructions in it. Let me read that file first.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":"d25a951e53f5a0126c41c7deea6704f76b44e8d9d6a94464438cff67d45316af"}]}}}}
